  "limitations": [
    "Six deterministic validation cases only; 33/55 bindings come from one case. No causal or population claim.",
    "Nearest downsampled hard pseudoGT and hard dense maps are sampling controls, not calibrated dense/coarse equivalence; tiny targets may vanish.",
    "Coarse hard A Dice uses argmax plus >=0.5; actual R consumes independent soft host masks, so both are reported.",
    "Single-crop dense A and whole-volume A are ungated by presence; R coarse A is multiplied by entity presence.",
    "Whole-volume inside/outside Dice averages different present-class sets and is not an additive decomposition.",
    "No relation logits under any substituted geometry have been computed.",
    "Tiny coarse-GT support is phase-sensitive: four lesions vanish under original nearest sampling, four/16 under fixed lower/upper center sampling. Coarse U IoU is descriptive and not a replacement for full-resolution matching.",
    "A large dense/coarse gap persists under all fixed sampling controls, but feature-coordinate alignment and continuous probability calibration have not been fully ruled out.",
    "Low whole-query IoU does not prove U training failure; a query can contain a useful separate component and instance information can be damaged by max/aggregation.",
    "All annotations are pseudo-references; six cases cannot establish causality or generalization."
  ],
  "next_single_variable_val_diagnostic": {
    "status": "proposed_not_executed",
    "name": "controlled R, replace only coarse A geometry input with same-crop dense predicted A probabilities",
    "population": "original full validation controlled-R set, all716 instances; no test selection",
    "replacement": "For the original selected query and crop, compute dense_p=sigmoid(entity_masks(out).float()); block-average dense_p over fixed (2,4,4) patch footprints to (64,40,40), cast to original coarse mask dtype, multiply the original native entity-presence sigmoid. Replace only the original coarse entity probabilities before host_masks_from_entities. Recompute geometry with the unchanged original coarse U, valid and coords, then call the unchanged relation head.",
    "fixed": "checkpoint; crop; input precision; embeddings/tokens; selected query ids; U masks/presence; query selection;14-host vocabulary; reference set; original B0; no training; no threshold search",
    "controls": "Baseline must reproduce; cohort and query ids/IoU remain fixed; emitted A and U predictions remain baseline-identical. Average pooling preserves small probability mass and matches the feature-grid footprint; never substitute nearest hard pseudoGT in the main comparison.",
    "readouts": "paired ABA(R), rescue/harm versus baseline R and unchanged B0, source/size/truth-host strata, geometry overlap/centroid/distance changes; report dense/coarse A support before and after",
    "interpretation": "A paired change tests sensitivity to A-geometry source on this fixed checkpoint. Null or adverse change does not exonerate A: coarse U and relation-head input-distribution mismatch remain. It is a diagnostic only and cannot count as a formal R pass or establish true human binding accuracy."
